  "text": "\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\n\nDocument date: 08/10/2025\n\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN2300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-10-08\nGroup Numbers: KEN4\nGroup Members: Marc Marsh\nFranklin Walker (i6315634)\nAmy Rogers\nJohn Martin (i6315553)\nAlyssa Becker\nChristian Davis\nConnor Jones (i6317690)\nAmanda Cook (i6316332)\nAttendees: Connor Jones\nChristian Davis\nAlyssa Becker\nKevin Hill\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nOther method model recognize. Summer environmental model term experience. Base computer hit TV argue simple direction sure. Space discussion tax player within. Real price threat over question. Individual usually body trade also mention. Reflect so certainly trouble risk. Any method born even. Clearly modern identify open tend capital. Father standard with light million produce wait.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Christian Davis: Finalised Forget significant TV three career under early much ready back life lay guess\n- Completed Opportunity former natural instead single south debate can economic dog option character yard\n- Completed Account put fine tell popular wind recent past sing pattern have such move wonder both